-- Infinite cardinal arithmetic: an infinite set is equipotent with its own
-- square, hence with its union or product with any set it dominates. Among
-- the bijections from the square of an infinite subset onto that subset, a
-- maximal one, which exists by the maximal principle since such bijections
-- are closed under nested unions, already covers the whole set.
-- Part of Cumulus, the Grace17 mathematics library.
-- Copyright (c) 2026 Grant Passmore.
